{title: How He loves us}
{artist: David Crowder}

{start_of_verse}
[C]He is jealous for me
[Am7]Love's like a hurricane, I am a tree
[G]Bending beneath the weight of his wind and [F]mercy.
When [C]all of a sudden,
I am unaware of these [Am7]afflictions eclipsed by glory,
And I [G]realize just how beautiful You are,
And how [F]great Your affections are for me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_prechorus}
[C]Oh, how he loves us [Am7]so,
Oh, how he [G]loves us,
How he loves us [F]so.
{end_of_prechorus}

{start_of_chorus}
Yea he [C]loves us,
Oh how he [Am7]loves us,
Oh how he [G]loves us,
Oh how he [F]loves.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
So [C]we are his portion and he is our prize,
[Am7]Drawn to redemption by the grace in his eyes,
If [G]grace is an ocean we're all [F]sinking.
So [C]heaven meets earth like an unforeseen kiss,
And my [Am7]heart turns violently inside of my chest.
I [G]don't have time to maintain these regrets
 when I [F]think about the way...
{end_of_bridge}

{title: Jesus have it all}
{artist: Jeremy Riddle}

{start_of_verse}
Intro: [Bb] [Dm] [C] [Gm]

1. Jesus have my [F]heart, my will, my soul
